# Workflow: Manually Removing Components & Wires

This workflow guides you (the AI Agent) through cleanly removing features, modules, or stubs from the codebase without leaving dead wires or compiler errors.

---

## Step-by-Step Removal Checklist

### Step 1: Remove Route Registrations
- Open `routers/main.go`.
- Delete the Fiber endpoints/group registrations associated with the component (e.g. remove `v1Group.Get("/products", ...)`).

### Step 2: Remove Dependency Wiring
- Open `internal/app/app.go`.
- Remove instantiations of the controller, usecase, and repository for that component.
- Delete any injections into other usecases.
- Clean up unused imports at the top of `internal/app/app.go`.

### Step 3: Delete Package Files
- Delete the feature directories:
  - `controllers/v1/[feature_name]/`
  - `usecases/v1/[feature_name]/`
  - `repositories/[db_type]/[feature_name].go` (or `repositories/[feature_name]/`)
  - `models/[feature_name].go` and `models/dto/[feature_name].go`
  
### Step 4: Run Code Analysis & Sync
- Execute `go mod tidy` in the terminal to remove unused third-party imports from `go.mod` and `go.sum`.
- Run tests (`go test ./...`) to ensure that no compile errors remain.
